    protocol = '''# Phase 05 — Preregistered variable comparison protocol\n\n## Scope\n\nProspective only. The VILD0 crosswalk is verified at airport-station-record level; exact sensor position and row-level source lineage remain unresolved. Apply only to future source-preserving, non-imputed data.\n\n## Shared rules\n\n- Preserve raw rows, provider/source IDs, timestamps, flags, units, retrieval settings, hashes and site metadata. Exclude model-filled, forecast, analysis, interpolated and imputed values. If row lineage is unavailable, mark `PROVENANCE_INSUFFICIENT`.\n- Convert timestamps to UTC without rounding. Exact timestamp joins are primary. Separately report one-to-one nearest matches within 15, 30 and 60 minutes; never reuse a neighbor observation. Preserve report validity times.\n- No filling; no zero inferred from missing; no missing-as-disagreement. Report variable-specific valid-pair counts and coverage before metrics.\n- Pragmatic descriptive minimum: 30 valid pairs on at least 10 distinct dates per variable. This is not a validated scientific threshold. Below it, show counts/distributions only and label estimates unstable. Event-level statements require at least 10 independent event episodes; repeated hours within one event are not independent events.\n- Report signed bias (neighbor minus primary), MAE, RMSE, median absolute difference and day-block bootstrap 95% intervals. Stratify by source pair, season, time-of-day and distance.\n- Numeric measurement tolerances and expected uncertainties are `NOT SPECIFIED` until instruments, resolutions, QC and agency/manufacturer performance specifications are identified. Do not make binary agreement claims before then. Once documented, preregister the specification-based primary tolerance and sensitivity at 0.5x, 1x and 2x that tolerance. These are sensitivity multipliers, not accuracy claims.\n- Agreement is measurement consistency, not independent corroboration. Investigate ownership and upstream source chains separately. Missing evidence is unavailable; contradictory evidence requires valid paired values and documented measurement uncertainty.\n\n## Variable plan\n\n| Variable | Units and alignment | Minimum | Metrics and tolerance | Limitations to resolve |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| Temperature | °C; exact UTC primary | 30 pairs / 10 dates | Bias, MAE, RMSE, median absolute difference, block CI; no fixed cutoff yet | Sensor accuracy, exposure, height, averaging, METAR rounding |\n| Dewpoint | °C; exact UTC primary | 30 / 10 dates | Same continuous metrics; no fixed cutoff | May be derived from temp/RH; establish derivation and dependence |\n| Relative humidity | %RH; differences in percentage points | 30 / 10 dates | Same continuous metrics; no fixed cutoff | Sensor response, temperature effects, derived values |\n| Wind speed | m/s after conversion; exact report time | 30 / 10 dates | Same continuous metrics; no fixed cutoff | Height, averaging period, exposure, units |\n| Wind direction | Degrees clockwise from north; exact report time | 30 valid non-calm pairs | Circular absolute angular error and circular bias; no fixed cutoff | Exclude calm/invalid flags; ordinary linear differences are invalid around 0/360° |\n| Pressure | hPa; exact UTC primary | 30 / 10 dates | Same continuous metrics; no fixed cutoff | Confirm station pressure vs sea-level/altimeter pressure and elevation reduction |\n| Precipitation | mm per documented accumulation interval; match interval endpoints | 30 paired valid intervals; report wet cases separately | Occurrence contingency metrics (POD, FAR, CSI) with counts; conditional amount bias/MAE/RMSE | Gauge type, trace coding, accumulation period; missing is not zero |\n\nNo fixed universal threshold is adopted. Exact-time results remain primary; tolerance-window results are separate sensitivity analyses.\n'''
    (OUT / "variable_comparison_protocol.md").write_text(protocol, encoding="utf-8")

