    report = f'''# Phase 05 — Primary Station Identity, Sensor Crosswalk and Site History Verification\n\n**Audit date:** 2026-11-18 UTC  \n**Branch:** `feature/phase05-primary-station-verification`  \n**Base checkpoint:** `7baf75a8a9682e611fb8a4b1cd248a1a6144cc65`  \n**Decision:** `VERIFIED_CROSSWALK` from VILD0 to the Ludhiana Airport (ICAO VILD) meteorological reporting station at station-record level. Exact sensor position and instrument lineage remain unresolved.\n\n## Executive finding\n\nThe traceable identity chain is Meteostat `VILD0` → ICAO `VILD` → Ludhiana Airport/Ludhiana Aerodrome meteorological reporting station. Meteostat lists VILD0 at 30.8547°N, 75.9526°E. NOAA NCEI's GHCNh station list contains `INI0000VILD` at those exact coordinates, elevation 254.2 m, name LUDHIANA; the Phase 1B Meteostat station database crosswalk links that GHCNh ID to VILD0. AAI identifies VILD as Ludhiana Airport and documents METAR reporting there. This verifies an airport-station crosswalk, not the exact sensor position or the source of every Meteostat row. [Meteostat VILD0 catalogue](https://meteostat.net/en/station/VILD0), [NOAA station list](https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/oa/global-historical-climatology-network/hourly/doc/ghcnh-station-list.txt), [AAI VILD eAIP](https://aim-india.aai.aero.in/eaip/eaip-v2-04-2026/eAIP/IN-AD%202.1VILD-en-GB.html)\n\nThe NOAA/Meteostat station coordinate is approximately **0.232 km** from AAI's aerodrome reference point (30°51′21″N, 75°57′02″E; 834 ft). That supports an airport-area location. The ARP is not a weather-sensor coordinate, so the NOAA point is retained as the station-record spatial reference only.\n\n## Crosswalk decision\n\n- **VILD0 → ICAO VILD: `VERIFIED_CROSSWALK`.** Meteostat explicitly associates VILD0 with VILD.\n- **ICAO VILD → Ludhiana Airport: `VERIFIED_CROSSWALK`.** AAI eAIP names VILD as Ludhiana Airport and identifies the aerodrome meteorological office.\n- **VILD0 → NOAA GHCNh INI0000VILD: `VERIFIED_CROSSWALK` at metadata-record level.** The Phase 1B provider crosswalk and exact match of NOAA coordinates/elevation support the link; NOAA's station-list row does not itself include ICAO VILD or row-level provider lineage.\n- **VILD0 → WMO 42099 equivalence: `NO_AUTHORITATIVE_MATCH`.** No authoritative alias/same-instrument link was found. The records have distinct identifiers; proximity or correlated values do not establish identity. Keep separate and do not substitute.\n- There is no evidence VILD0 is synthetic or manually assigned. “Ludhiana / Doraha” is a provider catalogue label, not proof that its instrument is in Doraha town.\n\nSee `vild0_identity_crosswalk.csv` and `crosswalk_evidence_log.csv` for full fields and limitations.\n\n## Historical acquisition and data provenance\n\nArchived exploratory/master notebooks report Meteostat 1.7.6 and retrieve `Hourly("VILD0", ..., timezone="Asia/Kolkata")` without setting `model` or `flags`. The official v1.7.6 source defaults are `model=True` and `flags=False`. Model filling was enabled and row-source flags were not requested. The saved series therefore cannot be certified as direct-only; individual rows cannot be separated into observed versus model-filled values. The notebook reports 45,229 rows from 2020-06-18 to 2026-03-09 and a separate 8,591-row extract. No flagged VILD0 raw export is present in Phase 04 outputs. [Meteostat v1.7.6 source](https://github.com/meteostat/meteostat/blob/v1.7.6/meteostat/interface/hourly.py)\n\nThe archived notebook inventory ended 2026-03-09, while the Meteostat page accessed 2026-11-18 lists availability through 2026-06-19. This is a changing provider inventory snapshot, not proof of a site move or direct-observation continuity. NOAA says GHCNh harmonizes observations from multiple sources, so the station ID alone cannot establish the source of each value. [NOAA GHCNh overview](https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/global-historical-climatology-network-hourly)\n\n## Site, measurement system and history\n\nAAI records the airport reference point/elevation and names Ludhiana Aerodrome as the meteorological office. Its GEN 3.5 tables list METAR and DIWE at the ATC tower; AAI defines DIWE as **Distance Indicating Wind Equipment**. This does not document the full temperature, dewpoint, humidity and pressure sensor suite. Exact instrument coordinates, exposure, make/model, calibration, installation dates, moves and provider changes were not established by the sources reviewed.\n\nAvailable AAI editions show reporting cadence changing from METAR “as required/as available” in 2018/2022 to hourly and half-hourly during hours of operation in 2026. This is an operational reporting change, not evidence of an instrument change. The full timeline is in `site_history_timeline.csv`.\n\n## Prospective comparison protocol\n\nThe accompanying protocol was set without tuning to neighbor comparison results. Exact UTC matching is primary; one-to-one 15/30/60-minute matches are separate sensitivity analyses. Missing values are not imputed or treated as disagreement. A pragmatic minimum of 30 valid pairs across 10 dates is set for descriptive metrics only, not as a validated scientific threshold. No numeric measurement tolerance is asserted because sensor specifications, resolutions and QC procedures were not identified. Variable units, metrics, missingness treatment and future sensitivity procedures are specified in `variable_comparison_protocol.md`.\n\n## E3 readiness\n\n**`PARTIALLY_READY`.** VILD0 now has a verified airport-station identity and a NOAA/Meteostat station-record coordinate for geographic referencing. Exact instrument position and source lineage remain uncertain. Phase 04 did not acquire a source-level VILD0 series, and historical notebook data may contain model-filled values with no row flags. Therefore validated primary-relative E3 comparisons cannot yet proceed. No zones were assigned and no Phase 04 output was modified. E3 remains **not validated**; identity resolution validates no anomaly/fault finding.\n\n## Source record\n\n`station_metadata_source_register.csv` records URLs, document names, retrieval dates, findings and limitations. The NOAA station-list snapshot retrieved 2026-11-18 12:39 UTC had SHA-256 `{NOAA_LIST_SHA256}`; its exact matching row is recorded in the register.\n\n## Follow-up gates\n\n1. Retrieve VILD0 with model inclusion, filling and cleaning disabled; retain per-row provider/source IDs or original METAR reports, retrieval settings and hashes.\n2. Obtain IMD/AAI station logs or an instrument inventory for sensor coordinates, variables, equipment, exposure, calibration and relocation history.\n3. Determine the provider/source for each historical Meteostat value before reusing the older dataset.\n4. Keep WMO 42099 separate absent an authoritative alias/site crosswalk.\n5. Run the preregistered primary-relative E3 protocol only after a provenance-complete VILD0 series is available.\n\n## Required outputs\n\n- `vild0_identity_crosswalk.csv`\n- `station_metadata_source_register.csv`\n- `site_history_timeline.csv`\n- `crosswalk_evidence_log.csv`\n- `variable_comparison_protocol.md`\n- `e3_readiness_assessment.json`\n'''
    (OUT / "PHASE05_PRIMARY_IDENTITY_REPORT.md").write_text(report, encoding="utf-8")
